rows.en:
I see...
Well then, it can't be helped.
I'll tell you.{p}

Can't you feel it?
The overwhelming aura filling this space...
It's slamming into me, wham, wham, so hard it hurts.{p}

...Shh!
Listen carefully...
Can't you hear a thin voice, sobbing?{p}

There was nothing.
The shoe locker was empty.
Forget a nice find, there weren't even any shoes or indoor shoes in it.{p}

".........Whoa, this is amazing!"
.........Hopeless.
He was completely lost in his own world.{p}

Honestly, why did Hino invite someone like this?
And honestly, why did I pick this guy first?
Cursing my bad luck, I hurried back to the club room with everyone.{p}

Oh?
How very reassuring.
That's the newspaper club for you.{p}

Aren't you the shy one.
Oh well.
So you're saying you'll walk there on your own.{p}

Creeeak...
The shoe locker's door swung open with a squeal.
Inside it was...{p}

"Oh? Now this is a nice find."
That's what he said...
Oh no, did I miss something?{p}

"What is it already?! You're so annoying."
How mean!
He could at least answer me.{p}

Ugh, he's so annoying...
If he doesn't like waiting, he can open it himself and come in.
And then...{p}

I sat down in my seat and made an effort to sound cheerful.
"Sorry to keep you waiting.
Now then, shall we move on to the next story?"{p}

Back in the club room, once I'd caught my breath, I looked straight into the eyes of the person I'd chosen earlier.
And I said this.
"Now then, the next story, please."{p}

